Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:34:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inventory): preserve authoritative Bedrock cartography
 results

Java cartography clears a received result whenever either input is empty, even while applying server inventory packets. Bedrock supports paper-only creation and map-only naming, so its valid results disappear in Java. Cancel local recipe recomputation only when native item context identifies a Bedrock menu.

Detect the existing ViaBedrock item component instead of the local protocol selection so the fix works through ViaProxy as well as direct connections. Keep recipe selection and requests in ViaBedrock core. Native inline naming and operation previews remain separate client rendering work.
---
 .../inventory/MixinCartographyTableMenu.java  | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../viafabricplus-bedrock.mixins.json         |  1 +
 2 files changed, 45 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/inventory/MixinCartographyTableMenu.java

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/inventory/MixinCartographyTableMenu.java b/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/inventory/MixinCartographyTableMenu.java
